foundation.question_text:
The number of water lilies on a pond was counted each week. The points and the fitted curve are shown. Find a model $y=kb^{x}$ for the number of lilies $y$ after $x$ weeks.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=-0.4,xmax=4,ymin=-3,ymax=48,xtick={0,1,2,3},ytick={0,5,...,45},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$ (weeks)},ylabel={Number of lilies},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0:3.1,samples=100] {5*exp(x*ln(2))};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,black] coordinates {(0,5) (1,10) (2,20) (3,40)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

development.question_text:
A rectangle has a fixed area. Its width $y$ centimetres was measured for several lengths $x$ centimetres, and the points and the fitted curve are shown. Find a model for the width $y$ in terms of the length $x$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=8.5cm,height=7cm,axis lines=middle,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=5.8,ymin=0,ymax=29,xtick={0,1,...,5},ytick={0,4,...,28},grid=both,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\small,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={$x$ (cm)},ylabel={$y$ (cm)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue!70!black,domain=0.9:5.4,samples=100] {24/x};
\addplot[only marks,mark=*,black] coordinates {(1,24) (2,12) (3,8) (4,6)};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
